WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.480
Our running case is a small outpatient clinic The
clinic needs to

00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:11.230
track patients providers appointments services and
the services delivered during each appointment

00:00:12.955 --> 00:00:17.402
Think about which words describe independent things
and which words describe relationships

00:00:17.415 --> 00:00:23.102
or rules Patient provider appointment and service
sound like candidate entities

00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:27.286
A rule such as every appointment must have a
provider sounds more

00:00:27.313 --> 00:00:32.420
like a constraint The design also needs to prevent
problems such as

00:00:32.446 --> 00:00:38.275
duplicate patient identifiers negative prices
impossible appointment times and service lists
stored

00:00:38.301 --> 00:00:44.064
as comma-separated text Before looking at the schema
try a quick warm-up

00:00:44.328 --> 00:00:47.985
which words in this scenario would you initially
consider tables and which

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:49.617
would you consider business rules
